---
import BaseHead from "@/components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="The Water Cooler News — Join the conversation, don't just listen"
      description="2-3 stories a week. The news your boss, colleagues, and clients are already talking about — so you can actually be part of it."
    />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <style>
      .font-instrument { font-family: 'Instrument Serif', serif; }
      .font-jakarta { font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="p-0 m-0 max-w-screen bg-white">
    <Header />

    <main class="container mx-auto md:px-10 px-4">

      <!-- Hero — dark background -->
      <section class="rounded-3xl bg-[#111] text-white my-6 py-20 md:py-28 px-6 flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-8">
        <span class="font-jakarta text-xs tracking-widest uppercase bg-pyellow text-black border-1 border-black/20 px-4 py-1.5 shadow-card1 rounded-sm font-semibold">
          Free · 2–3 times a week
        </span>

        <h1 class="font-instrument text-6xl md:text-8xl lg:text-9xl font-normal leading-tight tracking-tight max-w-4xl">
          The Water Cooler News <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 110" class="inline-block align-middle w-14 md:w-20 lg:w-24 h-auto -mt-2" fill="none">
            <rect x="27" y="2" width="26" height="7" rx="3.5" fill="#4BBFD6"/>
            <rect x="18" y="8" width="44" height="42" rx="6" fill="#A8C8E8"/>
            <rect x="18" y="46" width="44" height="7" rx="3.5" fill="#4BBFD6"/>
            <rect x="27" y="14" width="7" height="24" rx="3.5" fill="white" opacity="0.45"/>
            <rect x="28" y="52" width="24" height="8" rx="3" fill="#4BBFD6"/>
            <rect x="10" y="58" width="60" height="44" rx="8" fill="#E8EDF2"/>
            <rect x="10" y="69" width="60" height="9" fill="#B8C4CC"/>
            <rect x="18" y="84" width="18" height="9" rx="4" fill="#4A78C8"/>
            <rect x="23" y="93" width="8" height="7" rx="2" fill="#2C55A0"/>
            <rect x="44" y="84" width="18" height="9" rx="4" fill="#4A78C8"/>
            <rect x="49" y="93" width="8" height="7" rx="2" fill="#2C55A0"/>
            <rect x="25" y="102" width="30" height="6" rx="3" fill="#B8C4CC"/>
          </svg>
        </h1>

        <p class="text-base md:text-lg max-w-xl font-jakarta text-white/60 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Your boss knows about it. Your client mentioned it. Your colleague brought it up in passing.<br/><br/>Now you will too.
        </p>

        <!-- Beehiiv signup form -->
        <div class="w-full max-w-lg mt-2">
          <script is:inline async src="https://subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com/v3/loader.js" data-beehiiv-form="bb3975f0-50a6-4913-ab7d-3088abd75e80"></script>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs font-jakarta text-white/40 font-medium">Free. No spam. Unsubscribe anytime. Launching at 300 subscribers.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Divider -->
      <div class="border-t-1 border-black/10 my-4"></div>

      <!-- Value props -->
      <section class="py-16 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6" >
        <div class="border-1 border-black rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-pblue flex flex-col gap-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">💬</span>
          <h3 class="font-instrument text-2xl">Be in the conversation</h3>
          <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
            Not trivia. The actual news your boss, colleagues, and clients are already discussing — so you're adding to it, not catching up.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-1 border-black rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-pgreen flex flex-col gap-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">⚡</span>
          <h3 class="font-instrument text-2xl">When it matters, not daily</h3>
          <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
            2–3 times a week, only when there's something worth your time. A shorter version on stories. The full context here.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-1 border-black rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-ppink flex flex-col gap-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">🌏</span>
          <h3 class="font-instrument text-2xl">Global news, Indian lens</h3>
          <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
            Policy, geopolitics, and business — always connected back to what it means for someone working and living in India.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Sample issue -->
      <section class="py-8 pb-20 flex flex-col items-center gap-8" >
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 text-center">
          <h2 class="font-instrument text-4xl md:text-5xl">What it looks like</h2>
          <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack font-medium">A taste of what lands in your inbox</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Mock newsletter card -->
        <div class="w-full max-w-2xl border-1 border-black rounded-2xl shadow-card overflow-hidden">
          <!-- Newsletter header -->
          <div class="bg-pyellow px-6 py-4 border-b-1 border-black flex items-center justify-between">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 bg-black rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                <span class="text-white text-xs font-bold font-playfair">W</span>
              </div>
              <span class="font-playfair font-bold text-sm">The Water Cooler News</span>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 80 110" class="w-4 h-auto" fill="none">
                <rect x="27" y="2" width="26" height="7" rx="3.5" fill="#4BBFD6"/>
                <rect x="18" y="8" width="44" height="42" rx="6" fill="#A8C8E8"/>
                <rect x="18" y="46" width="44" height="7" rx="3.5" fill="#4BBFD6"/>
                <rect x="27" y="14" width="7" height="24" rx="3.5" fill="white" opacity="0.45"/>
                <rect x="28" y="52" width="24" height="8" rx="3" fill="#4BBFD6"/>
                <rect x="10" y="58" width="60" height="44" rx="8" fill="#E8EDF2"/>
                <rect x="10" y="69" width="60" height="9" fill="#B8C4CC"/>
                <rect x="18" y="84" width="18" height="9" rx="4" fill="#4A78C8"/>
                <rect x="23" y="93" width="8" height="7" rx="2" fill="#2C55A0"/>
                <rect x="44" y="84" width="18" height="9" rx="4" fill="#4A78C8"/>
                <rect x="49" y="93" width="8" height="7" rx="2" fill="#2C55A0"/>
                <rect x="25" y="102" width="30" height="6" rx="3" fill="#B8C4CC"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-pblack">Issue #1</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Content -->
          <div class="bg-white px-6 py-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
            <span class="font-jakarta text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-pblack bg-pblue/30 px-2 py-0.5 rounded self-start font-semibold">Policy + Geopolitics</span>

            <h3 class="font-instrument text-2xl leading-snug">
              Trump tried to end birthright citizenship on Day 1. His own Supreme Court said no. Here's why India already figured this out.
            </h3>

            <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
              On his first day back in office, Trump signed an executive order: being born on American soil no longer automatically makes you American. The Supreme Court rejected it as unconstitutional. But the conversation it started is worth understanding — because India had the exact same fight. Except we actually won it.
            </p>

            <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
              So what even is birthright citizenship? You're born on American soil, you're American. Full stop, kind of. Doesn't matter if your mum was there on a tourist visa or crossed the border the week before. Trump said people were flying in pregnant just to give birth there and game the system. So he signed the order. Funnily, his own Supreme Court appointees were the ones who rejected it.
            </p>

            <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
              Go back to 1947. The British leave, the country splits overnight, nobody asked anyone. Millions of Hindus and Sikhs are on the wrong side of a brand new border with nothing — no documents, no plan, just their lives. So the founding fathers did the obvious thing: if this is your home and Partition just put you on the wrong side of a line, come in. You belong here.
            </p>

            <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
              Then a new problem showed up from the east. People crossing into Assam from Bangladesh, having kids, those kids becoming Indian citizens automatically. Assam started feeling it heavily. So Parliament changed the law. 1987 — at least one parent needs to be Indian. 2003 — neither parent can be undocumented. Three moves over fifty years and India went from birthplace deciding citizenship to parentage deciding it.
            </p>

            <p class="font-jakarta text-sm text-pblack leading-relaxed">
              Trump needed to rewrite the entire American constitution to do what India did with three acts of Parliament. That's why he lost.
            </p>

            <div class="border-t-1 border-black/20 pt-4 mt-2">
              <p class="font-jakarta text-xs text-pblack italic">
                💬 Next time someone calls Trump's citizenship order radical: "India made the exact same move — three times. The difference is our constitution let Parliament sort it out."
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

      </section>

    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
